# colcon-cargo-ros2 generates all of this in-tree on every build.
#
# .cargo/config.toml carries [patch.crates-io] entries pointing at
# ../../../build/<pkg>/rosidl_cargo/, which are paths into this workspace's
# build directory — regenerated by colcon and meaningless anywhere else. It says
# "Do not edit" in its own header.
.cargo/

# Cargo.lock is NOT ignored: it is tracked on purpose. rclrs_image_transport
# asks for `rclrs = "*"`, so without a lock a fresh clone resolves it to the
# newest rclrs on crates.io (0.8) beside this crate's 0.7, and the build fails
# on two incompatible rclrs types (Phase 9, issue 7). The lock holds it at 0.7.
# It stays the same on every machine: colcon-cargo-ros2 0.5.3 stamps every
# generated interface crate 0.0.0 as long as no package in the workspace asks
# for one by version, so keep those requirements `*`.

# colcon per-package output
/build/
/install/
/log/

# cargo output — 2+ GB with the opencv bindings
/target/
